> show 1+2
_() = 3
  -> int
> show u8(255)+1
_() = 0
  -> u8
> show isqrt(x: u8)
_(x: u8) = isqrt(x)
  -> u8
> range isqrt(x: u8)
range of isqrt(x) -> u8:
  0..15   (16 distinct values)
  values: 0..15
  fits in u4
  over all 256 points of the domain
> parse sin(x)^2 + cos(x)^2
((sin(x) ^ 2) + (cos(x) ^ 2))
> diff sin(x)*x
d/dx sin(x)*x = x*cos(x) + sin(x)
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 3e-15)
> p(x: u8) = x+1
> q(x: u8) = 1+x
> equiv p q
p and q are equal on the domain of p (exhaustive)
